CLI|jdoe@inubit-dev-1.example.test> ps -h
usage: ps [OPTIONS] shows list of processes being in a certain state in the
          Process Engine.
Report a snapshot of the current queuemanager entries.
Options:
  -a,--all                               Shows all entries.
  -c,--count                             Shows only the number of matching
                                         processes.
  -csv                                   Use CSV output format instead of a
                                         table
  -e,--error                             Shows only processes in state 'Error'.
  -f,--filter <expression>               Defines a filter condition for show
                                         only process running states.
  -h,--help                              Displays this help
  -l <arg>                               Limits output to X rows.
  -q,--queued                            Shows only processes in state 'Queued'.
  -u <index>                             Show specified user defined column(s)
                                         as well. Leave blank to show all.
                                         Possible indices: 1..5
  -w,--waiting                           Shows only processes in state
                                         'Waiting'.
